  "id": "ipr",
  "term": "IPR",
  "definition": "IPR stands for Internal Psychological Retrenchment, a proposed process in which a person inwardly pulls back from heavy emotional investment in broad social competition. In this study, it is described as the psychological link between outside pressures and a state of tactical readiness within the broader pattern of strategic withdrawal called Ego-Tucking.",
